  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 6. Where the contamination comes from, weight by weight\nThe vector $(R\\otimes R)\\Psi_\\perp$, with $\\Psi_\\perp=(1-P_{\\rm HW})\\Psi$, has components only at weights $\\nu\\ge\\mu$, because $R$ raises. So\n$$\\text{contamination}=\\sum_{\\nu\\ge\\mu}c_\\lambda^{(\\nu)}\\cdot\\big[(R\\otimes R)\\Psi_\\perp\\big]_\\nu .$$\n`showContam[μ, copy, λ]` lists every nonzero term. For each it gives the $\\varepsilon$-power of $\\|c^{(\\nu)}\\|$ and of $\\|[(R\\otimes R)\\Psi_\\perp]_\\nu\\|$ (read off from the two values of $\\varepsilon$), and the term divided by the signal. The last rows give the $\\varepsilon$-powers of the signal and of $\\|\\Psi\\|$. Use it only where the signal is nonzero, i.e. not for $(1,1)$ at $[4,1,1]$ or $[2,2,2]$.\n\n**What to look for.** At $\\nu=[4,2,0]$, $c^{(\\nu)}$ is $O(1)$, because at $z=1$ the twist is trivial and $c_\\lambda\\propto e_1\\otimes e_1$. The signal's $c^{(\\mu)}$ is suppressed by powers of $\\varepsilon$, and $[(R\\otimes R)\\Psi_\\perp]_{420}$ is one order below $\\|\\Psi\\|$. The two products come out at the same order.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "εpow[a_, b_] := If[Abs[a] == 0 || Abs[b] == 0, \"-\", N[Log[Abs[b]/Abs[a]]/Log[εs[[2]]/εs[[1]]], 3]];\ncontam[μ_, copy_, λ_, ε_] := Module[{zv = zOf[ε], wv = wOf[ε], Ψ, c, Ψhw, rest},\n   Ψ = pickState[μ, copy, zv][\"psi\"]; c = cvec[λ, zv, wv]; Ψhw = PHW[μ] . Ψ; rest = RR[zv, wv] . (Ψ - Ψhw);\n   <|\"signal\" -> c . Ψhw, \"normPsi\" -> Norm[Ψ], \"terms\" -> Table[{ν, Norm[c[[secOf[ν]]]], Norm[rest[[secOf[ν]]]], c[[secOf[ν]]] . rest[[secOf[ν]]]}, {ν, Union[wtBasis]}]|>];\nshowContam[μ_, copy_, λ_] := Module[{A = contam[μ, copy, λ, εs[[1]]], B = contam[μ, copy, λ, εs[[2]]], keep},\n   keep = Select[Range[Length[A[\"terms\"]]], Abs[A[\"terms\"][[#, 4]]] > 10^-30 Abs[A[\"signal\"]] &];\n   Grid[Join[{{\"ν\", \"ε-power of ‖c^(ν)‖\", \"ε-power of ‖[(R⊗R)Ψ⊥]_ν‖\", \"term/signal, ε = 10^-3\", \"term/signal, ε = 10^-4\"}},\n     Table[{A[\"terms\"][[i, 1]], εpow[A[\"terms\"][[i, 2]], B[\"terms\"][[i, 2]]], εpow[A[\"terms\"][[i, 3]], B[\"terms\"][[i, 3]]], N[A[\"terms\"][[i, 4]]/A[\"signal\"], 6], N[B[\"terms\"][[i, 4]]/B[\"signal\"], 6]}, {i, keep}],\n     {{\"sum = κ - 1\", \"\", \"\", N[Total[A[\"terms\"][[All, 4]]]/A[\"signal\"], 6], N[Total[B[\"terms\"][[All, 4]]]/B[\"signal\"], 6]},\n      {\"ε-power of the signal\", εpow[A[\"signal\"], B[\"signal\"]], \"\", \"\", \"\"}, {\"ε-power of ‖Ψ‖\", εpow[A[\"normPsi\"], B[\"normPsi\"]], \"\", \"\", \"\"}}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]];\nshowContam[{3, 3, 0}, 1, \"21\"]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
