   "value": "## 7. Cancelling the contamination with $a+b\\,T_{(1,1)}+c\\,T_{(2,1)}$\nIn the frame with $R$ undone, the bare row $\\langle\\Omega|\\Psi\\rangle$ has covector $e_1\\otimes e_1$, which is pure top weight, because $\\langle\\Omega|=(e_1\\otimes e_1)^T(R\\otimes R)$. So the combination\n$$Q_v=a\\,\\langle\\Omega|\\Psi\\rangle+b\\,\\texttt{Qside}_{(1,1)}+c\\,\\texttt{Qside}_{(2,1)}=\\langle\\Omega|\\Psi\\rangle\\Big[a+b\\,\\frac{T^B_{(1,1)}}{f_{(1,1)}}+c\\,\\frac{T^B_{(2,1)}}{f_{(2,1)}}\\Big]$$\nhas covector $c_v=a\\,e_1e_1+b\\,c_{(1,1)}+c\\,c_{(2,1)}$, and everything from Section 5 is linear in $v=(a,b,c)$.\n- **Step 1: kill the top weight with $a$.** Set $a=-(b\\,c_{(1,1)}+c\\,c_{(2,1)})\\cdot e_1e_1=-3h^2z_2z_3\\,(b-h z_3\\,c)$, using the $[4,2,0]$ row of the Section 10d table. `vTop[{b,c}, d]` builds this $v$. Then the table gives $\\kappa$ for $(b,c)=(1,0)$ and $(0,1)$.\n- **Step 2: the singlet.** It also has contamination from intermediate weights. For the top-killed basis covectors, $K_b$ and $K_c$ are the contaminations and $S$ the signal of $c_{(2,1)}$; the signal of $c_{(1,1)}$ on the singlet is exactly 0. The ratio $\\beta=b/c=-K_c/K_b$ cancels the singlet's contamination.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* signal S, contamination K and top-weight component of the three basis covectors e1⊗e1 (bare Ω row), c_(1,1), c_(2,1) *)\nKS[μ_, copy_, ε_, φv_, ωv_] := Module[{zv = N[Exp[ε φv], pr], wv = N[Exp[ε ωv], pr], Ψ, Ψhw, rest, cs},\n   Ψ = pickState[μ, copy, zv][\"psi\"]; Ψhw = PHW[μ] . Ψ; rest = RR[zv, wv] . (Ψ - Ψhw);\n   cs = {kron[e1, e1], cλ[\"11\", zv, wv], cλ[\"21\", zv, wv]};\n   <|\"S\" -> (# . Ψhw & /@ cs), \"K\" -> (# . rest & /@ cs), \"top\" -> (# . kron[e1, e1] & /@ cs), \"z\" -> zv, \"sc\" -> Norm[Ψ] Max[Norm /@ cs],\n    \"Q\" -> {Om2[zv, wv] . Ψ, Qside[\"11\", Ψ, zv, wv], Qside[\"21\", Ψ, zv, wv]}|>];\n(* v = (a, b, c) with a fixed to kill the top-weight component *)\nvTop[{b_, c_}, d_] := {-(b d[\"top\"][[2]] + c d[\"top\"][[3]]), b, c};\n(* κ = Q_v / signal; \"CG = 0\" when the signal vanishes; \"0 = 0\" when Q_v vanishes too *)\nκv[v_, d_] := With[{s = v . d[\"S\"], q = v . (d[\"S\"] + d[\"K\"])}, Which[Abs[q] < 10^-40 d[\"sc\"], \"0 = 0\", Abs[s] < 10^-40 d[\"sc\"], \"CG = 0\", True, N[q/s, 8]]];\nchainResV[v_, d_] := Abs[v . d[\"Q\"] - v . (d[\"S\"] + d[\"K\"])]/d[\"sc\"];\naCheck = With[{d = KS[{3, 3, 0}, 1, εs[[1]], φ, ω]}, Max[Abs[{d[\"top\"][[2]] - 3 hN^2 d[\"z\"][[2]] d[\"z\"][[3]], d[\"top\"][[3]] + 3 hN^3 d[\"z\"][[2]] d[\"z\"][[3]]^2}]]];\n{tK, topTab} = AbsoluteTiming[Table[With[{A = KS[μc[[1]], μc[[2]], εs[[1]], φ, ω], B = KS[μc[[1]], μc[[2]], εs[[2]], φ, ω]},\n     {μc[[1]], μc[[2]], κv[vTop[{1, 0}, A], A], κv[vTop[{1, 0}, B], B], κv[vTop[{0, 1}, A], A], κv[vTop[{0, 1}, B], B],\n      N[Max[chainResV[vTop[{1, 0}, A], A], chainResV[vTop[{0, 1}, A], A]], 3]}], {μc, hwList}]];\nGrid[Join[{{\"μ\", \"copy\", \"κ, (b,c)=(1,0), ε=10^-3\", \"ε=10^-4\", \"κ, (b,c)=(0,1), ε=10^-3\", \"ε=10^-4\", \"chain residual\"}}, topTab,\n   {{\"a formula vs c_λ·e1e1\", aCheck, \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\"}, {\"time (s)\", tK, \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\"}}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
