  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 7b. Second chain point\nThe closed forms above were recognized from one chain point, so they are **pair-fitted** until checked elsewhere. `setPoint[h, θ]` changes the chain point and drops the memoized states and transfer matrices. The cell below repeats the singlet table at P2 = $(h,\\theta)=(1/3,(1/5,-4/9))$, which has $t=29/15$. It then tests the single combination\n$$v^*=\\big(a,\\ \\beta(t),\\ 1\\big),\\qquad \\beta(t)=h\\,\\frac{2t-3}{t-1},\\qquad a=-3h^2z_2z_3\\,(\\beta-h z_3),$$\non all six states at both chain points. Finally it restores P1.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "setPoint[h_, th_] := (hN = h; thN = th; θ12 = th[[1]] - th[[2]]; f11 = (θ12 - hN) (θ12 - 3 hN); f21 = (θ12 - hN)^2 (θ12 - 3 hN); fλ = <|\"11\" -> f11, \"21\" -> f21|>; u1 = thN[[1]] - 2 hN; u2 = thN[[2]];\n   DownValues[statesAt] = Select[DownValues[statesAt], ! FreeQ[#, Pattern] &]; DownValues[Tλ] = Select[DownValues[Tλ], ! FreeQ[#, Pattern] &];);\nvStar[d_] := vTop[{hN (2 θ12/hN - 3)/(θ12/hN - 1), 1}, d];\nstarTab[] := Table[With[{A = KS[μc[[1]], μc[[2]], εs[[1]], φ, ω], B = KS[μc[[1]], μc[[2]], εs[[2]], φ, ω]}, {μc[[1]], μc[[2]], κv[vStar[A], A], κv[vStar[B], B]}], {μc, hwList}];\n{tP, {starP1, singP2, starP2}} = AbsoluteTiming[{starTab[], setPoint[1/3, {1/5, -4/9}]; singTab[], starTab[]}];\nsetPoint[1/2, {2/7, -3/5}];\nColumn[{\n  Grid[Join[{{\"P2: directions\", \"ε\", \"K_b/S\", \"K_c/S\", \"β = -K_c/K_b\"}}, singP2], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left],\n  Grid[Join[{{\"μ\", \"copy\", \"κ(v*) at P1, ε=10^-3\", \"ε=10^-4\", \"κ(v*) at P2, ε=10^-3\", \"ε=10^-4\"}}, MapThread[Join, {starP1, starP2[[All, 3 ;; 4]]}], {{\"time (s)\", tP, \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\"}}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]}]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
