  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Results of Section 7 (2026-10-02)\n- **Killing the top weight with $a$ is enough for every state except the singlet.** With $a=-3h^2z_2z_3(b-hz_3c)$, both $(b,c)=(1,0)$ and $(0,1)$ give $\\kappa\\to1$ (deviation $O(\\varepsilon)$) for $[4,1,1]$ (only $(2,1)$; on $(1,1)$ both sides vanish), $[3,3,0]$, and both octets. Section 11g's $C$ is the special case $a=0$, which is why $C$ vanished on $[3,3,0]$.\n- **Octet mixing is fixed.** The two top-killed covectors have rank 2 on the octet HW space, so both octet HW states are determined up to scale by clean leading-order data.\n- **Singlet.** With the top weight killed, it still has intermediate-weight contamination. In units of the $(2,1)$ signal, it is $K_b/S=-(t-1)/(3h)$ for $c_{(1,1)}$ and $K_c/S=(2t-3)/3$ for $c_{(2,1)}$, with $t=\\theta_{12}/h$. It cancels for\n$$\\beta=b/c=h\\,\\frac{2t-3}{t-1}.$$\n  The forms were recognized at P1 ($-18/35$, $19/105$, $19/54$) and **validated at P2** ($-14/15$, $13/45$, $13/42$ predicted and observed). They are independent of $\\varphi$ and $\\omega$ (three direction pairs).\n- **One universal combination.** $v^*=(a,\\beta,1)$, i.e.\n$$\\langle\\Omega|\\Psi_B\\rangle\\Big[-3h^2z_2z_3(\\beta-hz_3)+\\beta\\,\\frac{T^B_{(1,1)}(\\theta_1-2h)}{f_{(1,1)}}+\\frac{T^B_{(2,1)}(\\theta_1-2h)}{f_{(2,1)}}\\Big]=c_{v^*}\\cdot h_\\mu\\,\\varepsilon^{-k}\\,(1+O(\\varepsilon)),$$\n  gives $\\kappa\\to1$ for all five non-top HW states at P1 and P2. $[4,2,0]$ is clean with any single $T_\\lambda$.\n- **Scope.** Only $[2,1,0]^2$, two chain points, $\\varepsilon\\le10^{-4}$, 80 digits. The $\\beta(t)$ formula rests on two points. It is singular at $t=1$, where $f_\\lambda$ vanishes anyway.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
